<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Heralds Research System · HRS v1.0</title>
  <%- include("partials/metadata") %>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>

<body class="hrs-site-page">
  <%- include("partials/header") %>

  <main>
    <section class="hrs-hero">
      <div class="hrs-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="hrs-hero-inner">
        <img
          class="hrs-stamp"
          src="/images/lionsbell-stamp.png"
          alt="Order of the Lion's Bell"
        >

        <p class="hrs-kicker">ORDER OF THE LION'S BELL · DIGITAL SYSTEM</p>

        <h1 class="hrs-title">HERALDS<br>RESEARCH SYSTEM</h1>

        <p class="hrs-version">HRS · VERSION 1.0 · ANDROID</p>

        <p class="hrs-intro">
          The research, archival and formation system of the Order.
          HRS brings the living work of the Heralds into one institutional record:
          research sources, investigations, correspondence, experience records,
          formation and the work of the Bell.
        </p>

        <div class="hrs-actions">
          <a class="hrs-action hrs-action-primary"
             href="/downloads/hrs-v1.0.apk"
             download>
            DOWNLOAD FOR ANDROID
            <span>›</span>
          </a>

          <span class="hrs-action hrs-action-disabled" id="google-play">
            GOOGLE PLAY · COMING SOON
          </span>
        </div>

        <p class="hrs-install-note">
          Direct Android distribution · signed HRS v1.0 build
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hrs-section">
      <div class="hrs-section-inner">
        <p class="hrs-kicker">ONE SYSTEM · ONE RECORD</p>
        <h2>THE WORK OF THE ORDER</h2>
        <div class="hrs-rule"></div>

        <p class="hrs-body">
          HRS is not a separate social platform. It is the working system behind
          the Order's research and institutional life. The website remains the
          public threshold; HRS is where records are organized, work is continued
          and member access is applied according to standing and responsibility.
        </p>

        <div class="hrs-grid">
          <article class="hrs-card">
            <span>I</span>
            <h3>RESEARCH ARCHIVE</h3>
            <p>
              The Heralds Research Library, sources, claims, evidence and
              structured archival records.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="hrs-card">
            <span>II</span>
            <h3>CASES & INVESTIGATIONS</h3>
            <p>
              Active files, submitted experiences, investigative records and
              formal research outcomes.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="hrs-card">
            <span>III</span>
            <h3>ORDER & FORMATION</h3>
            <p>
              Member record, formation progress, chapters, offices, Council
              records and advancement.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="hrs-card">
            <span>IV</span>
            <h3>THE BELL</h3>
            <p>
              Bell Reports, research correspondence and the publication record
              of work preserved by the Order.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hrs-section hrs-access-section">
      <div class="hrs-section-inner">
        <p class="hrs-kicker">ACCESS</p>
        <h2>ENTER THROUGH ONE IDENTITY</h2>
        <div class="hrs-rule"></div>

        <p class="hrs-body">
          The same HRS identity is used across the application and authenticated
          areas of the Heralds website. Seekers may enter the system with their
          own account; additional functions become available according to
          membership, standing, office and permissions.
        </p>

        <div class="hrs-secondary-actions">
          <% if (user) { %>
            <a href="/profile">VIEW MY ORDER RECORD</a>
          <% } else { %>
            <a href="/login">ENTER THE ORDER</a>
          <% } %>

          <a href="/archive">EXPLORE THE PUBLIC ARCHIVE</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%- include("partials/footer") %>
